On Feb 28, 1:33 am, "sevil...@gmail.com" <sevil...@gmail.com> wrote:

Here is how I handle potions.
> blindness, booze, fruit, healing, gain energy, hallu, invisibility,
> levitation (I expect a ring someday), monster&object detection, oil,
> paralysis, restore ability, see invisible, sickness, sleeping, speed
> (I expect boots).

blindness, fruit, hallucination, invisibility, sleeping, see
invisible,
monster detection, booze.
These get diluted for holy water. Invisibility waits
till I find make invisible. I keep one see invisible for blessing.

healing are upgraded by speed.

extra healing and full healing are upgraded by gain energy.

object detection is used on all levels with vaults.

oil is useful till there is a magic lamp, which is not guaranteed.

levitation is useful if ring or boots are not found.

paralysis is left alone for gehennom and endgame, when there
is a ring of free action.

restore ability will be diluted if not using pets which is after
finishing minetown and sokoban.

sickness is only useful if can use poisonable missiles.

Enlightenment are good for increasing Int and Wis.
But normally I upgrade full healing. They can also mix
with levitation to get gain level. Although both are not
very common.

polymorph can be used to dip extra unicorn horns
or elven cloaks or boots. But wands of polymorph
are much better.

confusion is good to keep around till you have expired
one spell. It makes a lot of sense to read any 1 or 2
lvl spellbooks if int+lvl/2 is near 20. Just make sure
that its not cursed, and you are mostly safe. You need
to have one that will expire as soon as possible. 20000
turns is still too long.

